fact WorkItem(id: "WI-257", description: some(value: "Shared NodeOccurrence tree-walk infrastructure. After WI-253/WI-254/WI-255/WI-256 we now have four iterative walkers over Rc<NodeOccurrence> trees with near-identical per-Expr-variant match logic: visit_classifications (node_occurrence.rs), collect_classified (req_insertion.rs), drain_expr_children (node_occurrence.rs Drop impl), plus the iterative typer's Visit dispatch (typing.rs). All except the typer share the same children-enumeration shape; the three push_children / push_classified_children / drain_expr_children helpers are ~50-line variant matches with only their per-slot body differing (push to stack vs steal vs visit-callback). Acceptance: introduce a single canonical for_each_child(expr, &mut |c|) helper (or into_children(expr) iterator) in kb/node_occurrence.rs that matches once per Expr variant; rewrite the three walker callers to use it; full workspace tests green. Approach: pre-walk and post-walk variants if both orders are needed; the destructive drain case in Drop needs a special owned-stealing variant (since direct Rcs need replacement with placeholders before the callback fires). Optional: encapsulate the work-stack pattern itself as a small Visitor combinator."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-16T15:27:41Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-257", author: "user", content: "Delivered as commit 57d0824. Single canonical for_each_child(expr, &mut |c|) in kb/node_occurrence.rs replaces the two structurally-identical push_*_children helpers in node_occurrence.rs (visit_classifications) and req_insertion.rs (collect_classified). Both walkers now call for_each_child with a 1-line stack-push closure. Net -54 LOC. Destructive drain_expr_children (used by Drop for NodeOccurrence) kept separate — it mem::take's Vecs wholesale and mem::replace's single-Rc fields with a Bottom placeholder, which is much cheaper than going through a per-child callback. Full anthill-core suite green via scripts/test.sh.", at: "2026-05-16T15:27:41Z")
